</p><p>This bill establishes a framework for sealing records related to certain federal criminal offenses.</p><p>Courts must automatically seal records related to (1) a conviction for simple possession of a controlled substance or for any nonviolent offense involving marijuana, or (2) an arrest for an offense that does not result in a conviction.</p><p>Additionally, an individual who meets certain criteria may petition to seal records related to a conviction for other nonviolent offenses.</p>","updateDate":"2026-10-06T21:29:33Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Clean Slate Act of 2025","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-10-06T21:30:16Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-10-06T21:30:16Z"}
